1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too,

3
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the carpenter
I was putting in a choke hold.

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Patsushiko Kameari,
one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water jug,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika, Shibamata,
losing even happiness again.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,700
Because I'm a fool who only
realized after listening.

13
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:31,480
The Volvo cohabitation era.

14
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:50,620
Right now

15
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,700
It really is peaceful, isn't it.

16
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,980
That's a good thing, isn't it?

17
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:55,800
Here's your tea.

18
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,020
Looking back now,

19
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:59,960
those wild,
dizzying days on Totten Hachibun-tō

20
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,280
That's why it's strange

21
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,240
Is that so?

22
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,700
You said you were already worn out,
didn't you?

23
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,740
What's wrong?

24
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,680
A strange man is coming this way.

25
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:12,700
A strange man, you say?

26
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,340
Who's that?

27
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,300
Well, it's Volvo!

28
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:23,480
Hey there, Volvo!

29
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,200
You're as bold as ever, aren't you.

30
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,700
You never know when someone
might attack you from behind.

31
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,440
Japan isn't that dangerous a place,
you know.

32
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,020
When did you come to Japan?

33
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,700
And that uniform...

34
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:41,980
Volvo, finally.

35
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,300
Starting today, as an instructor at
the Katsushika police shooting range,

36
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,840
I've been assigned to work there.

37
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:47,980
I see.

38
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,840
So that makes us colleagues, then.

39
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:50,820
Yeah.

40
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,780
I'm counting on you from here on.

41
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,480
Hidden guns

42
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:59,840
You're still carrying that much
weaponry even after coming to Japan?

43
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,280
No, that's all.

44
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,680
Really?

45
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:04,900
Really.

46
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,020
Then I'm going to check you.

47
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:12,280
See, there's this much here!

48
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:16,700
But as a police officer,
this much equipment is

49
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,080
This isn't New York or Tondemo Happun Island,
you know.

50
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:23,160
Look, look, this one's a baton gun.

51
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,280
It's like something from "The Toichi."

52
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,820
It really feels like a
weapons department store.

53
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,860
No, I'm just a timid guy.

54
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:35,700
What are you saying! As a police officer,
I'm here to protect the citizens!

55
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,040
No! It's all weapons to protect yourself!

56
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:43,100
Where in the world is there a
cop carrying a Motel Fullwort?!

57
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:44,900
Well, but...

58
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,800
What's all the commotion?

59
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:50,860
Don't come up behind me!

60
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:56,440
Ah

61
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:00,320
All your guns are right here, you know.

62
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,840
That's right.

63
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,940
Whenever someone comes up behind me, I just

64
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:06,380
That's why they call you a true nutcase.

65
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:09,560
Anyway,
tonight's Volvo's welcome party, right?

66
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,900
Agreed, agreed!

67
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:14,600
Yeah, we've got to teach Volvo
what Japanese common sense is.

68
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,740
Ryo-chan?

69
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:16,780
Meow

70
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,540
Meow

71
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,500
Well then, we'll be going.

72
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,740
Thanks for the meal.

73
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:25,900
Ryo-chan is

74
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:27,240
has fallen asleep.

75
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,000
Honestly, what a handful.

76
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,560
See you tomorrow.

77
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,740
Good night.

78
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,520
It's time.

79
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,020
What is it?

80
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:07,920
Who are you?

81
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,280
How far is it?

82
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,260
What's that helicopter?

83
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,780
It's taking twenty seconds to defend!

84
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,900
It's a bomber!

85
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:45,180
If they attack at the same time, we're dead!

86
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,480
Don't suddenly attack us in the
middle of the night like this!

87
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,880
Anyway, what did you come to Japan for?

88
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:54,560
My daughter Jodie has
taken a liking to Saigo.

89
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,040
Me?

90
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:57,500
Really?

91
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:01,220
The reason she beat you at
the Aramco candidate showdown

92
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:04,780
is that I heard Saigo is bad with women.

93
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:18,700
A chance!

94
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:27,000
My daughter really wants a rematch.

95
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,480
No way, you'll lose again.

96
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,320
So to get used to her,
you'll live with my daughter for a while.

97
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,640
Then face her again.

98
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,640
Live together.

99
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,180
Jodie and Volvo, are they...

100
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,160
Hey, Jodie!

101
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,760
Hi there, long time no see!

102
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,380
While our ship, the Carl Vinson,
is docked at Yokosuka...

103
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,980
I'll be living with Mr. Volvo,
my wonderful roommate.

104
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:54,920
Wonderful, you say?

105
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:58,120
Let me carry your luggage.

106
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:58,960
Thanks.

107
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,940
You're really going to
let them live together?

108
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:04,680
They're just roommates.
It's only sharing a place to live.

109
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:06,980
They're only roommates, Volvo.

110
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:08,700
Don't get any funny ideas.

111
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,480
I know, Shikkena.

112
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:14,460
Papa, I don't want to marry
a man who loses to a woman.

113
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:17,460
So let's fight again on equal terms.

114
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,960
Volvo, your nose is bleeding.

115
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:24,220
Sorry to rush, but can I take a shower?

116
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:25,620
A shower?

117
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,580
The shower's next to the entrance.

118
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,440
Right. Thanks.

119
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,240
Hey, hey, don't take your clothes off here.

120
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:36,080
What's the big deal?

121
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,600
Of course it's a big deal.
Change in the bathroom properly.

122
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,920
What a hassle.

123
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,700
Your daughter is way too bold.

124
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:48,080
She's American, so she's just open-minded.

125
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,800
She sometimes even walks around naked.

126
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,640
Pfft, a nosebleed!

127
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,680
Volvo, pull yourself together!

128
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:59,040
My daughter got 100% of her mother's blood.

129
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:00,200
By the way, this is

130
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,140
my wife.

131
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:03,780
Isn't she beautiful?

132
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:07,000
My wife's cooking is the best in the world.

133
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,580
And she works like a dynamo too.

134
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,380
She's the best woman.

135
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:11,820
Don't brag about your
family the American way.

136
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,140
Japan and America have
completely different cultures.

137
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,940
Especially if we're going to live together.

138
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,340
Having an international marriage,
I understand this well.

139
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:24,760
Suppose Saigo and my daughter got married.

140
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,720
You can't really tell in
this situation, though.

141
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,440
that it wasn't supposed
to turn out like this.

142
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,900
If you both regret it later,
it'll be too late.

143
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:35,260
That's why being roommates is the
best way to get to know each other.

144
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:38,740
Is it really all right for a father
to let his daughter live with a man?

145
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,580
It's my daughter's decision.

146
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:43,000
Jodie has been independent
since she was fifteen.

147
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,760
She's been living on her own, after all.

148
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:48,200
In Japan, even university students still
haven't left their parents, have they?

149
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:52,180
Besides, the culture is different.
She's very independent.

150
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:54,280
That's how it is, apparently. Got it?

151
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:56,480
Finally, that's settled.

152
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,860
Could you lend me a bath towel?

153
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:08,460
At least take a towel
with you when you go in.

154
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:09,820
Thanks.

155
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,900
I'm heading home.

156
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:18,020
Hey, what about your daughter?

157
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:20,760
Not my problem.

158
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,020
This cold is incredible.

159
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:33,100
Seriously, what an outrageously annoying old man,
showing up at three-thirty in the morning.

160
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:35,080
Are you okay, Volvo?

161
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:38,020
It feels like I'm having a nightmare.

162
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,880
That was a nice bath.

163
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,800
Volvo, get changed and come out, will you?

164
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,200
What's the big deal, anyway?

165
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:53,760
The talking just won't stop.

166
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,020
So that's why you came home at dawn, senpai?

167
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,540
I can't keep up with this.

168
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:06,520
A guy who's never even held a woman's
hand is suddenly living with one.

169
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,700
And she's a blonde with huge tits.

170
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,240
The gap is huge.

171
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:10,920
Right?

172
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,260
Isn't her father worried, I wonder?

173
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,700
He's a total individualist, after all.

174
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:19,220
On top of that, Jodie is a crew member
on the aircraft carrier USS Carl Vinson.

175
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:22,600
Since she lives among
wrestler-like soldiers,

176
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,940
she's probably become more manly than a man,
don't you think?

177
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:27,320
You've got a point.

178
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:30,360
Volvo and the others should
be waking up about now, right?

179
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:32,920
Shall the three of us go check on them?

180
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,920
Do you think Volvo's all right?

181
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:42,520
Maybe he bled to death from that nosebleed.

182
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:46,440
It's scary that he isn't dead, really.

183
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:52,820
Isn't that Volvo over there?

184
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,160
That's definitely Volvo.

185
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:04,220
He went and slept outside
to be considerate to Jodie

186
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:08,400
Serves him right. What a handful!

187
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:14,200
Are you awake? Nakagawa and Reiko came by,
worried about you.

188
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:15,940
Hey.

189
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:20,160
Stop hanging around out
there and let us in already.

190
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:21,800
Understood.

191
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,020
Uh-oh.

192
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:36,800
Jodie!

193
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,680
Something happened, didn't it?

194
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:51,700
Were you sleeping naked?

195
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:55,340
No, it got hot in the middle of the night,
so I took my clothes off.

196
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:58,280
That's the same thing!
Put your clothes on already.

197
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:03,700
But if he's going to build up his immunity to women,
it's better for him to see everyday life like this, right?

198
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:08,040
Volvo's immunity is on par with a middle schooler's.
Think a little before you act!

199
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,380
Honestly, you're such a hassle.

200
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:15,700
Volvo-san! Are you all right? Volvo-san!

201
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,200
Looks like he got an eyeful.

202
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,000
He must have been really shocked.

203
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,460
What a troublesome couple.

204
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,940
This is dinner?

205
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:47,220
You said you'd make dinner to apologize for this morning, so we came,
and this is what we get.

206
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:50,240
It's all military canned food

207
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:54,400
I thought so.
But it's really delicious, you know.

208
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,820
Bobby's happy to eat it, too.

209
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:57,400
No.

210
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:02,700
Showing off like newlyweds already,
with Bobby?

211
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:04,200
No, that's not -

212
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:04,380
No way!

213
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:08,260
It's like a wild animal's meal,
but I'll take it anyway.

214
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,980
You're hopeless at cooking anything but canned food,
aren't you?

215
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,620
I can do that.

216
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:15,160
Really?

217
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,860
It's cooking with wild boar or bear.

218
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,920
I was the best at survival training.

219
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,600
You hang whatever you
want to catch with a rope.

220
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,420
First, you skin it.

221
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,900
Then you pull out the innards,

222
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,980
and scrape the meat off the bones to eat it.

223
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,140
It's delicious.

224
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,797
Here you go. Hare is delicious too.

225
00:13:36,847 --> 00:13:39,200
It tastes like chicken.
The thighs especially.

226
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,128
Th-that sounds delicious.

227
00:13:42,178 --> 00:13:45,180
If we get the chance next time,
please do let us have some.

228
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:48,580
Well, I suppose it's about time I head home.

229
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:51,140
Yes, we've kept you for quite a while.

230
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,660
Well then, Pawlbo.
Make sure you do your best.

231
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:55,660
See you.

232
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:56,840
Good night.

233
00:13:57,060 --> 00:14:00,340
You're really leaving?
Please stay until morning.

234
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:04,240
I'm going to watch the all-night
Drifters comedy marathon now.

235
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,320
No way...

236
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:06,820
Bye-bye.

237
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:10,000
You've got to make a life together with Jodie,
you know.

238
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:13,520
Yes, after all, she's your roommate now.

239
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:16,420
Yes, Bobby.

240
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:19,020
The carrier sails in just five days,
you know.

241
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:23,500
We have to help Bobby get over his fear of women,
no matter what.

242
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:24,620
I'll do my best.

243
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:25,700
Well then.

244
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:26,860
Sorry for intruding.

245
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:27,840
Bye-bye.

246
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:29,000
Bye-bye.

247
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:31,220
He's gone.

248
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,440
Volvo...
we've got to do something about him.

249
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:34,400
Yeah, you're right.

250
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:37,620
And they're so in love, too.

251
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:43,840
Looks like it's just the two of us now

252
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,920
Yeah.

253
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,700
Jodie-san...

254
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,960
Bobby, you don't have
to push yourself so hard.

255
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:54,820
No, it's fine.

256
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:59,100
I said earlier that we
only have five days left,

257
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:03,980
but we still have five whole days, right?
So let's just get some sleep tonight.

258
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:05,680
S-sleep?

259
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,660
Of course, separately!

260
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:09,840
R-right, of course.

261
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,020
